{"chunk_id": "d84206089259", "text": "In this episode, Duryodhana\u2019s scheme to destroy the Pandavas unfolds. Knowing the sage Durvasa\u2019s terrifying temper, he sends the ascetic and his ten thousand disciples to visit the exiled Pandavas after Draupadi has already eaten\u2014when their magical vessel can no longer produce food. Durvasa arrives, and Yudhishthira dutifully welcomes him, asking him to bathe before dining. Panic grips Draupadi, who realizes there is no food to feed such a vast host. In desperation she prays to Krishna. Krishna appears, asks for food, and finds a single grain of rice in the vessel. After eating it, he mystically satisfies the hunger of the entire universe. When Durvasa and his disciples bathe, they suddenly feel completely full and flee in fear of offending the Pandavas. The episode highlights divine intervention, Draupadi\u2019s devotion, and the protection granted to those who trust in Krishna.\nDurvasa and thousands of disciples visit the exiled Pandavas; Draupadi prays to Krishna, whose miracle fills the sages so they flee before eating.\nThemes: divine intervention, hospitality duty, devotion to Krishna, danger from Durvasa, exile of Pandavas", "vector": [0.01590627245604992, -0.029179783537983894, 0.011161815375089645, 0.019060103222727776, -0.0021511176601052284, 0.021432330831885338, -0.014932699501514435, -0.02307780832052231, -0.023818273097276688, -0.016948407515883446, 0.025655722245573997, 0.0003008136700373143, -0.002581341192126274, 0.00726066529750824, -0.011470342986285686, 0.018607597798109055, 0.04909005016088486, -0.020102238282561302, 0.03041389025747776, -0.02846674434840679, -0.005090693011879921, -0.005008419044315815, 0.0065887621603906155, 0.03647473081946373, -0.01967715658247471, 0.014918986707925797, -0.0002553916710894555, -0.015522328205406666, 0.0067258854396641254, -0.0023705146741122007, -0.011367499828338623, 0.0021048386115580797, 0.018223652616143227, -0.0029241489246487617, -0.0131363878026604